.TH IMGVIEW 1 "" "imgview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imgview, iv \- image viewer for close inspection of pixels and EXIF metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imgview
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iv
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imgview
shows an image scaled to the window. When zoomed in it shows the stored
pixel values unmodified (nearest neighbour) by default, and it can invert
colors and adjust gamma to make faint features easier to spot. An info panel
shows the file size, dimensions and EXIF metadata.
.PP
.I path
may be an image file or a folder; for a folder, its first image is opened.
The left and right arrow keys then step through the folder's images. Without
a path, a file picker opens.
.B iv
is a short alias for
.BR imgview .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B + = \-
Zoom in, zoom out (the mouse wheel zooms around the pointer).
.TP
.B 0
Fit the image to the window.
.TP
.B r
Zoom to exactly 1:1, centred on the pointer.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Pan a zoomed image (with Shift: by one image pixel). Left and right switch
to the previous and next image in the folder when there is nothing to pan
sideways.
.TP
.B i
Toggle zoom-in resampling between nearest (true pixels) and bicubic.
.TP
.B n
Toggle color inversion.
.TP
.B . , /
Gamma up (darker), gamma down (brighter), reset gamma.
.TP
.B m
Show or hide the info panel.
.TP
.B o
Open an image with a file picker.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave fullscreen; otherwise quit.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/JCallicoat/imgview
